","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-23T00:58:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:42:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n- Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.5.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M4 Pro (14 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using an EXR file as a `Sprite`, the sprite will appear dark.\n\nThe problem is resolved by enabling HDR 2D in the Viewport project settings.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Drag an EXR file into a 2D scene to create a `Sprite`.\n2. Notice that the EXR file is rendered too dark.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n<img width=\"1176\" height=\"690\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9d6cef2-2873-4516-b7d2-98a7bf612fd5\" />\n\nIn the following project, both the EXR and PNG file contain the exact same image and should render identically:\n[exr-dark.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29228744/exr-dark.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120562/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120562/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}